# Goal: rank candidate motion plans by VLM-assessed risk.
# `candidates` are in the local (base_link) frame of the observation identified
# by `header`, so the server scores them against the exact scene they were
# planned on.
std_msgs/Header header
nav_msgs/Path[] candidates
string task
# Where the robot is trying to get to, as [x, y] in the same frame as
# `candidates`. Per-query data: it tracks the planner's carrot, so it moves every
# cycle. EMPTY means the client has no goal to offer; the server then scores on
# safety and forward progress alone and draws no goal marker.
float32[] goal
---
# Result: per-candidate risk, aligned index-for-index with the goal's candidates.
#
# SUCCEEDED with a full risk[] is the only usable outcome. ABORTED means risk
# could not be assessed this cycle (no camera frame, no calibration, or a VLM
# failure); the caller must fail closed and requery rather than selecting a
# candidate risk-blind. CANCELED means the caller withdrew the request.
float32[] risk
# Metres of each candidate, from its start, whose ground was observed unoccluded in the
# frames this assessment was made from. Index-aligned with risk[] and the goal's
# candidates. EMPTY means the server does not compute it: the caller must fall back to
# its own commitment bound rather than truncating to zero.
float32[] visible_length
float64 elapsed
---
# Feedback: wall-clock seconds spent executing this goal so far.
float64 elapsed
